  "note": "Triennial election of Lisburn Urban District Council, polled on Monday 15 January 1923 in the South Ward only. The North Ward (5 seats, 5 candidates) and Central Ward (6 seats, 6 candidates) were walk-overs; the paper lists those returned unopposed. 5 seats, 5 candidates, returned unopposed; Shortt and Barnes new councillors. Returned unopposed."
